{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaqipKne9Jut2nF5wGkD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I proved `reverseAcc_fusion` in `Main.lean`. `lean Main.lean` ran with no errors or warnings, so the proof checks.\n\n```lean\ntheorem reverseAcc_fusion (xs ys acc : List α) : reverseAcc (xs ++ ys) acc = reverseAcc ys (reverseAcc xs acc) := by\n  induction xs generalizing acc with\n  | nil => rfl\n  | cons x xs ih => exact ih (x :: acc)\n```\n\nThe proof is by induction on `xs`, with `acc` allowed to vary:\n- **`nil` case:** both sides simplify to `reverseAcc ys acc` by definition, so `rfl` closes it.\n- **`cons` case:** both sides unfold to the claim for the shorter list `xs` with accumulator `x :: acc`. That is exactly the induction hypothesis at `x :: acc`. The hypothesis has to work for any `acc`, which is why `generalizing acc` is needed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_read_input_tokens":7963,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491},"output_tokens":334,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94eaa662-b54b-4b87-84ff-a2eb7c720f25","uuid":"a7d29e92-7b39-4f5d-9267-42bcf374d95d","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:08:26.922Z","request_id":"req_011Cgaqip4ugTFtv2HHH6X7Y"}
